    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p20-q7-construction-group",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "",
        "prompt": "By switching $A$ and $C$ if necessary, we can assume that $\\angle ABD\\leq\\angle CBD$. Let $P$ denote the point on $AC$ such that $\\angle CBP=\\angle ABD$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p20-q7-a",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "a",
            "prompt": "Show that $\\triangle DBA\\sim\\triangle CBP$ and $\\triangle CBD\\sim\\triangle PBA$.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\triangle DBA\\sim\\triangle CBP$ and $\\triangle CBD\\sim\\triangle PBA$ (AA).\n\nUse equal angles on the same arc and the constructed equality $\\angle CBP=\\angle ABD$.",
              "worked": "Since $P$ lies on $AC$, angles on the same arc give $\\angle BCP=\\angle BCA=\\angle BDA$. Also, $\\angle CBP=\\angle DBA$ by construction. Hence $\\triangle DBA\\sim\\triangle CBP$ (AA).\n\nAngles on the same arc give $\\angle BAP=\\angle BAC=\\angle BDC$. At $B$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\angle CBD&=\\angle CBP+\\angle PBD\\\\\\angle CBD&=\\angle ABD+\\angle PBD\\\\\\angle CBD&=\\angle PBA.\\end{align*}$$\nHence $\\triangle CBD\\sim\\triangle PBA$ (AA).",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 60
          },
          {
            "id": "p20-q7-b",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "Conclude that\n$$AC\\times BD=(AD\\times BC)+(AB\\times CD).$$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$AC\\times BD=(AD\\times BC)+(AB\\times CD)$.\n\nMultiply the similarity ratios by $BD$ and use $AC=CP+AP$.",
              "worked": "The similarity relationships give\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{PC}{BC}&=\\frac{AD}{BD}\\\\PC\\times BD&=AD\\times BC\\\\\\frac{AP}{AB}&=\\frac{CD}{BD}\\\\AP\\times BD&=AB\\times CD.\\end{align*}$$\nAdding, and using $AC=CP+AP$,\n$$\\begin{align*}(CP+AP)\\times BD&=(AD\\times BC)+(AB\\times CD)\\\\AC\\times BD&=(AD\\times BC)+(AB\\times CD).\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 70
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
